documentation
ui
	^ 'Spec UI:
- HSKSpec: main ComposablePresenterWithModel. initializeWidgets creates the exercises notebook and opens Pinyin Reminder and Pinyin Attack pages; subMenu builds a menu; start and stop delegate to the attack; modelChanged forwards the model to every page; defaultSpec is one column with exercises. The menu instance variable is never assigned.
- HSKPinyinReminder: ComposablePresenterWithModel. Widgets: AthensStaticPresenter word (100x100), meanings text, pinyin text input (autoAccept), Accept, Hint, Give up and Inspect buttons, status text, and todo/done ComponentListPresenters of HSKCharacterProfile. acceptEntry validates a non-empty pinyin, calls exercise current assertWith:, sets result #right or #wrong, shows the expected pinyin and advances; hintNeeded shows the current hint; giveUp shows the pinyin, submits a give up and advances; inspectCurrentChar inspects the current exercise; privateNext advances and refreshes lists; loadData clears the input and refreshes meanings and lists; modelChanged creates SRSPhoneticExercise goal: model; startup calls modelChanged. Layout methods box, grid, bodyGrid and table use legacy Spec layouts; defaultSpec answers box.
- HSKPinyinAttack: ComposablePresenterWithModel with a text entry and an AthensAnimatedPresenter viewport (900x500). A Timeline drives ticks; drawOn: clears the canvas and draws the character 好 at 20@tick with PingFang TC 30; start forks a loop while animating, ticking and waiting 50 ms; stop terminates the process; updateModelTo: stores the tick and refreshes.
- HSKCharacterProfile: presenter with character, level and result labels; model: an SRSKnownContent, skill: and result:; drawCharacterOn:box: draws through HSKDrawableContent with PingFang TC 5 (the Athens label code is commented out).
- HSKDrawableContent: content and font; drawOn:at:font: translates the canvas and draws content asHSKString traditionalString.'